@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture;design] ios-host-renders-shared-compose
The iOS host MUST render the shared Pully Compose controller. It MUST NOT duplicate
Pully screens or business rules in Swift. Native code MAY adapt system lifecycle,
authentication, storage, links, input, navigation and device services. Source: Tavi,
21 Oct 2026, chosen Compose Multiplatform implementation with maximum Android reuse.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] ios-preview-is-explicit
The iOS app MUST identify itself as an internal preview until the complete account,
review and AI journeys are connected and validated. The ordinary live host MAY read
its configured server only through the actual shared account/client and secure native
adapters; a restored session MUST be verified first. Deterministic nonprivate fixtures
MUST require an explicit Debug launch switch, with a fixture label, and MUST NOT replace
live server/account errors. Unsupported mutation, review and AI controls MUST remain
unavailable before work starts. Source: Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 full iOS implementation and
the accepted staged live-account/Home activation after the first fixture milestone.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture;design] ios-bundled-locales-match-web
The iOS app bundle's `i18n/` JSON locale set and each file's bytes MUST equal
`packages/app/src/i18n/locales`. The host MUST package the existing Android mirror
without maintaining another set of translation files. Source: Tavi's 21 Oct 2026
maximum-reuse iOS decision and DESIGN.md's locale source-of-truth enforcement.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture;design] ios-feedback-is-native-output-of-shared-cuelume
iOS control feedback MUST synthesize the existing shared Cuelume recipes and DSP.
Native code MAY adapt PCM output and system haptic generators, but MUST NOT replace
the cue signatures with generic system sounds. It MUST respect the saved sound and
haptic preferences, Ring/Silent, and suspension; suspended feedback MUST NOT replay
on resume. Source: Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 maximum-reuse iOS decision and Android
sound-follows-the-phone, sound-cue-per-role and DESIGN.md rule 125.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] ios-keychain-tests-use-real-private-app-identity
The iOS Keychain roundtrip MUST execute the actual secure-store adapter in a
genuine app-hosted simulator test with its own private application identifier in
the code-signed executable. The harness MUST verify the built signature and the
actual matching XML/DER simulator entitlements embedded in that executable,
MUST NOT widen Keychain sharing, and MUST NOT skip or mock a missing entitlement
as a passing result. Source: Tavi's chosen 21 Oct 2026 native-storage plan and
the real simulator errSecMissingEntitlement failure; Apple DTS app-host guidance
and Xcode's simulator entitlement representation observed in the 21 Oct Mac run.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture;security] ios-home-services-follow-actual-scene-lifecycle
Shared Home actions MUST use native clipboard writes and external HTTPS GitHub
navigation, bypassing the app's incoming-link router. Lifecycle registration MUST
synchronously report the current scene state, then real scene transitions;
cancellation MUST remove exactly that registration, and disconnection MUST stop
and release all observers. An obsolete reentrant foreground event MUST NOT resume
background work. Source: Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 maximum-reuse plan and shared Home
NativeHomeActions contract, preserving Android foreground lifecycle ownership.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture;motion] ios-edge-back-drives-shared-navigation
The iOS leading-edge recognizer MUST report normalized progress and commit or cancel
to the existing shared PageMotion and navigation stack. It MUST use the shared
layout direction, reject disabled root navigation, cancel on scene interruption,
and release replaced or cancelled registrations. It MUST NOT transform the native
controller or maintain another route stack. Source: Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 maximum-reuse
iOS plan and the shared NativeHomeActions edge-back integration decision.
The one recognizer MUST receive both the root Compose view and its sibling dialog
layers in the same scene window, while a presented native controller MUST prevent
the underlying shared route or sheet from consuming its gesture. Source: the real
21 Oct 2026 simulator sheet-dismissal failure and the same shared Back priority.

A registration created before the root acquires its window MUST be retried when the
scene becomes active; repeated attachment or activation MUST NOT add a second edge
recognizer for that registration. Source: the accepted 21 Oct 2026 native Back
continuity repair after actual simulator repository and dialog journeys.
The shared Back recognizer MUST retain native Back prevention priority while a
Compose dialog is open, so the framework's click-only Back handler cannot swallow
its progress gesture. The same scene/root/presentation and shared-consumer gates
MUST still decide whether it starts or commits. Source: the actual 21 Oct 2026
modal-only simulator failure and pinned Compose 1.12.2 Dialog/navigation input.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture;security] ios-explicit-browser-uses-native-web-presentation
The shared explicit browser action MUST accept only HTTP(S) URLs with a host and no
URL credentials, and MUST present the native browser controller from the active
scene. Its initial navigation MUST bypass Pully and GitHub universal-link routing.
The separate open-on-GitHub action MAY use direct system navigation. Neither action
MAY forward Pully RPC or Access credentials. Source: Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 maximum-reuse
iOS plan and the shared Overview browser action through NativeHomeActions.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] ios-live-account-uses-secure-native-adapters
The scene's account storage host MUST adapt the existing private Keychain store and
registered native Google flow without implementing account RPCs. A source mutation
MUST deliver synchronous old-owner invalidation before the new snapshot is readable,
then publish its completed notification. Native selection cancellation MUST detach
on MainActor even when the coroutine was cancelled on another dispatcher. A locked
or corrupt store MUST offer retry/reset without issuing anonymous RPCs. Source:
Tavi's 21 Oct 2026 full iOS implementation request and accepted account adapter plan.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] ios-live-simulator-tests-use-the-real-app-identity
The real Pully simulator host MUST retain a private ad-hoc application identity before
running account bridge or UI tests that use Keychain. CI MUST first retain unsigned
compilation, verify the actual signed executable and its matching exact private XML/DER
claims, then execute the original UI tests and actual app-hosted account bridge tests.
Simulator entitlements MUST NOT apply to device builds or widen credential sharing.
The dedicated native Keychain test MUST remain mandatory. Source: Tavi's 21 Oct 2026
full iOS implementation request, ios-keychain-tests-use-real-private-app-identity,
and the actual unsigned simulator errSecMissingEntitlement diagnosis.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:architecture;security] ios-scene-retains-one-live-application
The scene MUST retain one shared application owner above ordinary routes and native
browser presentation. Scene disconnection MUST close its account, source caches,
settings work, analytics, subscriptions and lifetime scope before releasing native
services. Failed application construction MUST release already-created resources.
Source: the accepted 21 Oct 2026 native host lifetime and single Compose-stack plan.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] ios-root-fixture-uses-isolated-real-native-storage
The actual-root simulator fixture MUST require an explicit Debug launch selection
with a validated unique UUID. It MUST use a separate preferences suite and the real
app-private Keychain adapter under its own service, retain that same service for
restore validation, and never adopt ordinary credentials or standard preferences.
Fixture preference changes MUST NOT delete or alter ordinary usage queues. Ordinary
launches MUST retain the actual Darwin transport and secure account owner. Source:
the accepted 21 Oct 2026 native account/Home/review fixture validation plan.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product;architecture] ios-cold-and-warm-links-use-one-shared-inbox
Cold scene URL contexts and browsing activities, and their warm scene callbacks,
MUST feed the retained shared application's incoming-link inbox after native Google
callbacks are handled. Invalid native envelopes MUST use the same current-source
shared error path once; they MUST NOT become placeholder destinations or log their
input. Scene disconnection MUST retire delivery before closing the application.
Source: Tavi's accepted 21 Oct 2026 native/shared link and single-stack plan.
@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:product] ios-journey-tests-observe-the-production-filter
The native Home journey tests MUST tap the actual production filter control and
assert its exported selected state. A matching text descendant or parent container
MUST NOT stand in for that control. The tests MUST retain the existing row, native
Back, scroll and foreground continuity assertions. Source: Tavi's accepted 21 Oct
2026 real iPhone journey plan and DESIGN.md rules49/128 on accessible state and
retained navigation context.

@cc [owner:OctavianTocan,label:security;architecture] ios-complete-services-share-source-and-installation-policy
The complete native host MUST install the existing shared review, Analyze, Tour,
Brief, Chat/history and Inbox surfaces with one retained Settings model owner and
one source-owned Home/Review tour-copy adapter. Temporary verification or scene
pause MUST restrict fresh actions without replacing the installed renderer policy,
private drafts or accepted-write owner. Ordinary scene close MUST preserve tour
files for verified reopening; a true source change MUST revoke writers and purge
its active namespace before replacement credentials are published. Explicit Debug
journeys MUST use only their validated UUID's separate tour directory, retain the
strict read-only mode and keep unsupported fixture RPC controls unavailable.
Source: Tavi's accepted 21 Oct 2026 complete maximum-reuse iOS journey and native
source/lifecycle isolation plan.
